 "description": "The Ro-Go was a Japanese heavy tank design that joined the trend of multi-turret tank designs such as the T-28 , T-35 , and the Independent . While it was the second Japanese tank that was adopted for service after the Type 89 I-Go , its combat trials in Manchuria proved that the production, cost, weight, and mobility were problems and resulted in not seeing mass production. The Ro-Go was introduced in Update 1.67 \"Assault\" . It plays very closely to the I-Go , lacking any real armour, offering a low-velocity main cannon that does have a potentially strong HEAT shell and lacklustre mobility. The additional benefits however include an additional 37 mm in a secondary turret, a rear machine gun operated by an independent crew member that helps survivability, and overall more crew members in total.",
